<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill yield eases to 13.56 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill yield eases to 13.56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of Kazakh three-month MKM discount Treasury bills edged down to 13.56 percent at an auction on Tuesday from 13.82 percent at the last auction on July 29, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   Aug 5		July 29</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K0611972     KZ43K3010974</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  700		  600</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 2,425		1,639</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 700		  600</p>
<p> Average price			 96.72 pct	  96.66</p>
<p> Average yield			 13.56 pct	  13.82</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Nov 6, 1997	Oct 30, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +8 3272 509410</p>
</text>
